p.src:
This is where burnout and judgment meet. A founder who says yes to every possible interaction is not being generous with an infinite resource. He is spending a finite one. The practical doctrine from Lecture 111 is therefore: $\text{protect the reserve}
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
\text{say no to non-value-adding demands}.$

